  "summary": {
    "intent": "Manage a batch of open PRs/CI on oxc-react-codegen, resolve a Dependabot conflict, assess TS 7.1 prep status, and rewrite ADR/architecture docs to be clear and agent-friendly — then propagate those documentation/memory-boundary learnings to sibling repos (callisto, agent-plugins, wisp).",
    "outcome": "Verified all four PRs green and explained the Dependabot rebase behavior; assessed TS 7.1 readiness (three fixes landed, semantic backend not started, RDT oracle broken); researched ADR best practices and the ADR/AGENTS.md/memory boundary, then applied it: wrote ADR 0006, rewrote type-checker-integration.md, renamed CLAUDE.md→AGENTS.md repo-wide, added ADR README index/guardrails, pruned stale project memory files, and wrote a 'Next step' section plus a starter prompt for a fresh session to fix the RDT oracle.",
    "learnings": {
      "repo": [
        "apps/validate's RDT oracle crashes on import against typescript ^7.0.2 (ts.JsxEmit undefined); RDT 2.4.0 needs a TypeScript 6 API (typescript@6 or @typescript/typescript6), separate from the typescript@next build used by the semantic probe.",
        "Claude Code >= 2.1.277 reads AGENTS.md only when no CLAUDE.md exists in the working directory or above; if both exist, only CLAUDE.md loads unless it has an @AGENTS.md import.",
        "The validation harness only compares name, required, type, and default, and renders types itself — narrower than docs implied.",
        "crates/core/AGENTS.md still describes the DTS cache as mtime+size invalidation; the code actually uses a content hash (not yet fixed).",
        "docs/benchmarks.md is a stale 2026-07-25 report whose 'outliers dominate structural bucket' claim can't be re-verified until the RDT oracle is fixed.",
        "oxc dependency is now 0.151 (memory/doc references citing 0.135 were stale)."
      ],
      "code": [
        {
          "path": "crates/cli/Cargo.toml",
          "finding": "watchexec-signals dependency (added in PR #16) sits adjacent to comfy-table/crossterm lines that Dependabot's PR #10 bumps, causing a textual (non-semantic) merge conflict."
        },
        {
          "path": "docs/adr/0006-semantic-backend-as-second-resolver.md",
          "finding": "ADR records running RDT's algorithm on tsc --api merged into the structural result; trimmed after review to decision/why/constraints/alternatives only, removing volatile cost numbers (ms, MB) and dates that belong in type-checker-integration.md instead."
        }
      ],
      "workflow": [
        "ADRs should record only architecturally-significant, hard-to-reverse decisions plus rejected alternatives and the causal 'because' — not measured costs, timelines, or enforcement/process scaffolding (Enforcement/Revisit-when/Sources sections, 'Proposed until implemented' status, superseded/ folders) which are conventions from other repos (callisto), not core ADR practice per Nygard/MADR.",
        "For agents specifically, ADRs matter because an agent with no memory will silently reverse a structural decision by reading only the code — the rejected alternative and reason must reach the agent before it edits, via routing from AGENTS.md to an ADR index.",
        "Clear content-type boundary: ADR = architecture/direction decisions; AGENTS.md = session rules/conventions (committed, cross-agent); specs = required behavior; docs = current-state description; agent memory = personal/uncommitted preferences and corrections; commit message = why one change was made.",
        "Repo conventions (comment style, commit style) belong in committed AGENTS.md, not personal memory, especially when other agent tool configs (.codex, .cursor, .gemini, .opencode) exist and can't read Claude's memory.",
        "Before citing repo facts in docs, verify them against actual code/config rather than relying on prior assumptions (caught several stale/incorrect claims this way)."
      ]
    },
    "friction": [
      "A background CI-wait task notification reported 'failed' when it had actually succeeded — the failure was just grep exiting 1 on no matches, causing a false alarm.",
      "The callisto repo's working tree changed mid-investigation (restructured docs while being read), requiring a re-survey.",
      "Scratchpad/probe scripts were purged by environment cleanup/compaction between sessions, requiring recreation of the parity probe.",
      "Auto-mode classifier denied force-deleting three stale local branches, leaving manual cleanup to the user.",
      "Untracked AGENTS.md copy in the repo had @crates/*/AGENTS.md imports pointing to files that didn't exist, silently making it dead weight until discovered."
    ],
    "open_items": [
      "Fix the RDT oracle in apps/validate by pointing it at a TypeScript 6 API, separate from the typescript@next build.",
      "Commit the parity probe script into apps/validate instead of leaving it in the scratchpad.",
      "Re-run parity probe against full fixture corpus once oracle is fixed; extend beyond the 13 hand-picked components.",
      "Build a Rust client for the lifecycle gate (timeout/crash/staleness fixtures) — not started.",
      "Add core contract/reconcile step: PropType variant and schema version field — not started.",
      "Decide on and change branch protection's 'CI' setting (deferred to user).",
      "Local branch deletion (fix/ts7-lib-resolution, fix/child-interface-prop-override, wip/session-work) deferred to user.",
      "Decide on bigger diagnostics-lifecycle change (snapshot() keeping first extraction's diagnostics, update_file running plugin hooks) — deferred to user.",
      "Fix crates/core/AGENTS.md's stale claim that DTS cache uses mtime+size (actual: content hash).",
      "Re-verify docs/benchmarks.md's outlier-dominance claim once oracle is fixed.",
      "Apply agent-plugins fixes (CLAUDE.md @AGENTS.md import, new decision-records.md reference, comments.md line 15 split, ranger adversary.md dual-file check) — briefed to a new agent, not yet executed.",
      "Apply wisp changes (first-class decision artifact/schema, memory-boundary statement, artifact precedence rule, CONTRIBUTING.md/CI references to nonexistent AGENTS.md and just docs-lint, hard-wrapped docs) — explicitly out of scope/deferred as separate task.",
      "Uncommitted changes to AGENTS.md/CLAUDE.md renames, ADR 0006, ADR README, and docs remain on main branch — user was advised to branch before committing (two proposed commits: ADR+index, then AGENTS.md rename+references)."
    ]
